## a11y

Node `a11y` supports `progressbar`, `meter`, `status`, and a local semantic-node
`controls` relation (Anima extensions without inventory rows). Progressbar/meter use
numeric bound `value`, min/max (defaults 0/100); omit progressbar value for indeterminate
progress. Status defaults to polite live announcements. `controls` maps to `aria-controls`.
Dialog `modal` and button/link/group/list-item `expanded` already accept bool literals,
inputs or data paths. `anima docs a11y` includes recipes; `anima schema a11y`
shows the complete registry vocabulary. These are node fields, separate from root §10 a11y.

Node semantics are specified in [modules/a11y/SPEC.md](../modules/a11y/SPEC.md). Interaction,
diffs and focus policy live in the companion `a11y-actions` (runtime key `a11yactions`); in-browser
AniML forms in the `markup-a11y` web entry. The optional `a11y-dom` web entry supplies the platform overlay,
including canvas positioning through the optional canvas backend's node-box adapter. Synthesized
semantic focus targets use world geometry-box centers; directional candidates exclude ancestors
of the current target. Unchanged semantic reads reuse retained dependencies before collecting the
scene. Geometry/visibility, binding and owner dependencies govern recollection; paint-only changes and
unchanged list steps preserve it. See the module contracts and `spec/conformance/a11y-spatial-focus`. Root §10 is unchanged.

<!-- capability: a11y.tree-bounds -->
### Semantic bounds

`nodes[].a11y.bounds` (AniML `bounds`) is a local `[x,y,w,h]` box with nonnegative width and height,
transformed to world-grid coordinates. Without it, visible child boxes are unioned
for unpainted groups; an empty node reports its transformed origin as a point.
The bounded implementation and explicit path/stroke limitations are specified in
[modules/a11y/SPEC.md](../modules/a11y/SPEC.md). This row remains planned.


<!-- capability: a11y.property-heading-level -->
### Heading hierarchy

A node with `a11y.role: "heading"` accepts `level` as an integer 1–6 or a
number input/data path. AniML uses `<a11y role="heading" level="2"/>`; a bound
level uses a JSON string attribute, for example `level="&quot;depth&quot;"`.
Bound values must remain integers 1–6. Unknown names report `unknown-input`,
wrong types `input-type`, and invalid literal levels `bad-value`, at that field's
JSON pointer. See [the node semantics contract](../modules/a11y/SPEC.md), its
`a11y-property-heading-level` conformance case and paired capability example.


<!-- capability: a11y.focus-condition -->
### Focus transition condition

With `a11y-actions` and `focus`, a machine guard operand `{ "focus": "id" }`
is true for the primary target and focusable semantic ancestors. Documents without
node semantics retain exact-target focus conditions. The existing machine guard
registry and AniML JSON `guard` attribute own both spellings and unknown-target
validation. See `spec/conformance/a11y-focus-condition` and
[the node semantics contract](../modules/a11y/SPEC.md). Repeated targets are covered by the module tests; six native PNG stages independently verify
ancestor conditions, as recorded in the closure report.

### Node semantics

Static labels, explicit boxes, simple painted groups, state bindings and queued actions
are available. Exact path/stroke bounds and several focus policies remain unfinished;
see REPORT.md. The fixed budgets pass after the bounded fixes.

```xml
<anima version="0.1" name="mute" grid="20" requires="a11y focus">
  <bool name="muted"/>
  <rect id="mute" x0="2" y0="2" width="16" height="16" fill="#000">
    <a11y role="checkbox" label="Mute" checked="muted" bounds="2 2 16 16"/>
  </rect>
</anima>
```

Use `anima validate`, `anima schema circle.a11y`, and
`anima sample file.animl --semantics -e 'semantic mute tap\nsnapshot'`.
For a slider bind value to a number input or data path and set min/max/step.
Use value-text for independent spoken text, either a literal or a string data path.
See examples/slider-value-text.animl for `$volume` plus a derived `$volumeText`
that speaks "Volume 40 %". Anima has no standalone string inputs. Bind text or states
to `$path` only when data is declared and loaded. Semantic tap toggles a bound
checked/pressed/selected bool unless activate explicitly names a bool or trigger.
Traits follow from role/states; do not write trait bits. Root `<a11y>` is unchanged.

See [SPEC.md](SPEC.md) for the tree contract, diagnostics and remaining gaps.


For static labels/roles load only `@anima-format/web/a11y` (add `@anima-format/web/markup-a11y` when the page compiles AniML in the browser). For interaction and
focus policy load `@anima-format/web/a11y-actions` (which imports that base entry),
plus the optional focus module when needed. The runtime key for the companion is
`a11yactions`. The CLI registers both automatically. Core hosts import `a11y` and
`a11yActions` from their respective entries and register both. `semanticDiff` is now
exported by `@anima-format/core/a11y-actions`.

Read-only semantic controls and bindings to read-only data (for example list length)
expose focus when eligible, but no edit actions. Multiple taps before a step queue
multiple toggles. A group without explicit bounds unions its visible child boxes;
use explicit bounds for paths/strokes until their exact extents are implemented.

`semantics mute` prints only that subtree. `snapshot --semantics $path` combines
semantic inspection with a filtered values snapshot. Omitted bool states are false
for platform consumers; traits are derived and are never authored or serialized.

With logical focus on a semantic control, headless keys use its native behavior:
`semantic volume focus`, `key down ArrowRight`, `key up ArrowRight`. Space needs
a down/up pair; button/switch/link Enter activates on down. Tab-list arrows/Home/End
rove enabled tabs. Numeric range actions compose before a step and respect both
semantic and input/data limits. Repeated targets use `rows.0.item`; author
`<focus edge="parent-scope"/>` on the repeat to leave a row at its child edge.


#### Tab list: selection follows focus

Arrow/Home/End keys rove focus; selection is explicit. Bind each tab's `selected` to a bool and
handle its focus event to set the selection, so keyboard focus and selection agree:

```xml
<anima version="0.1" name="tabs" grid="20" requires="a11y focus">
  <bool name="first" default="true"/><bool name="second"/>
  <group id="tabs">
    <a11y role="tab-list" label="Views"/>
    <rect id="one" x0="0" y0="0" width="8" height="8" fill="#000">
      <a11y role="tab" label="First" selected="first"/>
    </rect>
    <rect id="two" x0="10" y0="0" width="8" height="8" fill="#000">
      <a11y role="tab" label="Second" selected="second"/>
    </rect>
  </group>
  <listener on="focus" target="one" set="first=true"/>
  <listener on="focus" target="one" set="second=false"/>
  <listener on="focus" target="two" set="first=false"/>
  <listener on="focus" target="two" set="second=true"/>
</anima>
```

Check with `semantic one focus`, `key down ArrowRight`, `expect second == true`.
Apply the same selection writes to your panel visibility bindings. Keep disabled tabs out of the
selection; arrow navigation skips them. Explicit focus listeners also cover pointer/host focus.

#### Progress, status and controlled dialogs

These are **node** semantics (`<a11y>` inside a node), not the smaller root accessibility block.
`anima schema a11y` lists every node role and state. `modal` (dialog/alert-dialog) and
`expanded` (button/link/group/list-item) are existing bool literal/input/data-path fields;
the downstream kit's claim that expanded/modal are unavailable was a discoverability gap.

```xml
<anima version="0.1" name="progress" grid="40" requires="a11y">
  <number name="amount" default="40"/>
  <bool name="open"/><bool name="closed" default="true"/>
  <group id="loading"><a11y role="progressbar" label="Loading" value="amount" min="0" max="100"/></group>
  <group id="waiting"><a11y role="progressbar" label="Waiting"/></group>
  <group id="capacity"><a11y role="meter" label="Capacity" value="amount"/></group>
  <group id="message"><a11y role="status" label="Ready"/></group>
  <group id="opener"><a11y role="button" label="Details" expanded="open" activate="open" controls="panel"/></group>
  <group id="panel"><a11y role="dialog" label="Details" modal="open" hidden="closed"/></group>
</anima>
```

Omit progressbar `value` for indeterminate progress; meter requires a number binding.
Status announces label changes politely. `controls` names another semantic node in the same
component and becomes `aria-controls`; it does not open, focus or reveal that node.
Use a separate bool input/data property for `hidden` (state fields accept bindings, not expressions).
Modal dialogs suppress semantic siblings while active; manage entry/return focus explicitly.
CLI `semantics` and `snapshot --semantics` expose these roles and relations, and
`anima sample file.animl --semantics` includes them without a browser.

### Node accessibility

The fixed per-entry budgets are reported in REPORT.md. Root document `a11y` in SPEC §10 retains its
existing shape, validation and behavior. See REPORT.md for remaining gaps.

#### Authoring

Every node can have `a11y`, declared with `requires: ["a11y"]`, or an AniML
`<a11y …/>` child. Registry entries in `core/registry.ts` own both spellings.

| JSON field | AniML attribute | Values |
|---|---|---|
| role | role | button, checkbox, switch, radio, radio-group, slider, tab, tab-list, link, list, list-item, group, dialog, alert-dialog, heading, text, img, none, progressbar, meter, status |
| label, hint, value | same | literal string or `$path` string data binding; slider/meter value requires a number input/path; progressbar value is optional and numeric when present |
| valueText | value-text | slider/progressbar/meter: literal string or `$path` string data binding; spoken value independent of numeric value |
| level | level | integer 1–6 or number input/data path; heading only; bound AniML values are JSON strings (`&quot;depth&quot;`) |
| href | href | string; link only |
| controls | controls | local id of another node with a non-none a11y role; maps to aria-controls |
| checked | checked | bool literal, bool input name or `$path` |
| checkedMixed | checked-mixed | bool literal/input/path; checkbox only; true overrides checked with `mixed` |
| pressed, selected, expanded, disabled, hidden, required, readonly, modal | same | bool literal/input/path |
| live | live | off (default), polite, assertive |
| activate | activate | trigger input (fire), or bool input (toggle) |
| min, max, step | same | min/max for slider/progressbar/meter, step for slider only; defaults 0, 100, 1; min < max, step > 0 |
| bounds | bounds | local [x,y,w,h]; nonnegative width and height; defaults to painted bounds |

